# issue #81 (unsat-shaped variant). X ⊑ ∃r.∃s.Y, Range(r,F), DisjointClasses(F,W),
# ∃s.Y ⊑ W: the r-successor must be F (range) and, once it also witnesses
# ∃s.Y, W (via the second axiom) — F and W are disjoint, so X is unsatisfiable.
# unsatconj.ofn is the FLAT (non-nested) sibling that rustdl gets right.
provenance: hermit
unsatisfiable: X
